{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789223050,"nonce":"huA3XqBnHxnacZJs6Kqj8Z1QBe8=","title":"A short-circuit and/or nested inside another expression crashes the backend","message":"`print(True and False)`, `print(1 \u003c x \u003c 10)` (a chained comparison\ndesugars to and), and `x if a and b else y` all fail with\n\"Call instruction: arg HirId(N) not in value_map\" at\ncranelift_backend.rs:2549. The and/or lowering builds a diamond and\nleaves control in its merge block via continuation_block; the enclosing\nCall (and Binary, Unary, Cast, any consumer of a sub-expression) keeps\nemitting into the block it started in, so the call precedes the phi that\ndefines its argument. Third site of the defect fixed for the ternary and\nthe CFG CondBranch in 1cd88f7; the fix should be general: after\ntranslating each operand, continue in continuation_block if set.\n\nConformance: bool/logic.py, compare/chained.py,\ngrammar/conditional_expression.py.","files":null}]}